{"type":"say","text":"Thank you both, Ravi and Mei. I appreciate the thoroughness and the recommendation to hold. I agree that we should not record a final decision today — the compliance condition on the quarterly independent valuation requirement remains unverified, and our normal pre-meeting process calls for complete documentation before I record a decision.

To summarize where we stand: Ravi has disclosed the conflict-of-interest finding to this committee, which satisfies the disclosure condition of our conflict policy. However, the second condition — confirmation that the fund contract requires quarterly independent valuation — has not yet been verified. Mei has provided a clear cash management check-in confirming that we can support a $5,000,000 commitment while preserving the $3,000,000 reserve, but not the full $8,000,000 requested.

Ravi, please proceed with your review of the fund contract and formally add both the ownership filing finding and the contract review to the committee packet. Mei, please ensure your cash forecast memo is circulated alongside Ravi's documentation. Once both of those are complete and Ravi has confirmed the contractual valuation requirement, I'll reconvene to record my final decision. If the quarterly independent valuation requirement is confirmed in the contract, I'm prepared to approve a $5,000,000 commitment with the conflict disclosed on record. If it is not confirmed, I will decline the commitment outright. We are adjourned for now."}
